  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-89251\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p></p><p>First, let's rewrite the phrase \"The dress is red and elegant\" as the equivalent phrase \"The dress is red and the dress is elegant.\" The sentence now reads</p><p></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The dress is red and the dress is elegant, and it is elegant.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Then, using the associative law, we can move the comma:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The dress is red, and the dress is elegant and it is elegant.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Now, we can simplify the phrase \"the dress is elegant and it is elegant\" to just \"the dress is elegant.\" The sentence now reads</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The dress is red, and the dress is elegant.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Finally, we can write the sentence more concisely as</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"The dress is red and elegant.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>",
